  "provenance": "UNOFFICIAL third-party mirror of a DLD export. The file is exactly 1,048,575 rows, which is Excel's 1,048,576-row ceiling, so it is a TRUNCATED copy of the registry. Coverage ends in 2023.",
  "period": "2000–2023",
  "minSalesPerYear": 30,
  "method": "For each community the annual median price per m2 is computed for every year with at least 30 priced residential sales. The layer reports the deepest fall from any running annual peak to a later year — the worst drawdown that community has actually experienced. Requires at least 6 scored years.",
  "limitation": "A volatility and downside-risk measure, not a forecast, and it says nothing about where prices sit today. Annual medians are affected by shifts in the mix of units sold, so part of a measured fall can be composition rather than price. Only the years the truncated export covers are searched.",
